Phase 1.8: Doc Fetch     → main session (Context7 MCP) — skip if no external libs detected
Phase 1.9: Probe Gate    → main session (Risk-First Integration Probe rows before fan-out)
Phase 2: Implementation  → inline units and executor units with explicit integration
Gate 2:  Validation      → validator — retry up to 3× on FAIL
Phase 3: Testing         → tester
Gate 3:  Coverage        → measure; enforce only a declared threshold
Phase 4: Review          → reviewer + security-auditor — retry up to 2× on REQUEST_CHANGES
```

`auto pipeline run` dispatches five phases on the full route — `plan`,
`test_scaffold`, `implement`, `validate`, `review` — and only `implement`,
`validate`, `review` when one valid change contract and the actual changed paths
authorize the compact route, where test-first work is folded into the
implementation step. It prints `Pipeline route: compact|full — <reason>` and
records `route_phase_set`; report that set as-is. Phase 1.9 is in-session gate
work bounded by the `risk_first_probe` decision, not a dispatched phase.

@AX annotation is not a phase. It runs only when the user asks for it or the run
